.TH TASKSCOPE 1 "October 2026" "Taskscope 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taskscope \- lightweight task manager and system monitor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskscope
[\fIoption\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Taskscope shows running processes, performance graphs for the processor,
memory, disks, network adapters and graphics adapters, plus installed
applications, startup applications, users, services and kernel drivers.
It reads the kernel's /proc and /sys files directly and uses whatever tools
the distribution provides for everything else, falling back to alternatives
when one is missing.
.PP
With a display and a Qt binding (PySide6, PyQt6, PyQt5 or PySide2) it opens a
window; otherwise it runs as a terminal application. One window runs per
user; starting the program again raises it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Use the terminal interface.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print the backends detected on this system and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-remote [\-\-host ADDR] [\-\-port N]
Serve a read-only, token-protected summary page without opening a window.
.TP
.B \-\-screensaver [\-root | \-window\-id ID] [\-\-audio]
Run the live-load screensaver.
.TP
.B \-\-register\-screensaver [\-\-no\-open]
Add the screensaver to ~/.xscreensaver.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-settings
Delete the settings file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Exercise every backend (and the GUI when available); exit 0 on success.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/taskscope/settings.json
Settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TASKSCOPE_QT
Force a Qt binding: pyside6, pyqt6, pyqt5 or pyside2.
